KDOS Add-ons — what is in the set, and under which licence
=============================================================

Everything in the set is distributed under the MIT licence below.

KDOS's own work, copyright KDOS contributors:

    the four wallpapers (org.kdos.scanlines, org.kdos.blueprint,
      org.kdos.horizon, org.kdos.eight), drawn by genaddons.py in the KDOS
      accent colours
    the VGA colour schemes, from the IBM VGA text-mode palette
    the KWin scripts org.kdos.pinpip and org.kdos.activescreen
    the widgets org.kdos.plasma.phosphorclock and org.kdos.plasma.focustimer
    the Konsole and KDE colour-scheme files of every palette below, which
      genaddons.py writes from that palette's published colours

The palettes the colour schemes are made from, each under the MIT licence:

    Nord              Copyright (c) 2016-present Arctic Ice Studio and Sven Greb
                      https://www.nordtheme.com
    Dracula           Copyright (c) 2016 Dracula Theme
                      https://draculatheme.com
    Gruvbox           Copyright (c) 2012-present Pavel Pertsev
                      https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox
    Tokyo Night       Copyright (c) 2021 Folke Lemaitre
                      https://github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim
    Catppuccin        Copyright (c) 2021 Catppuccin
                      https://github.com/catppuccin/catppuccin

Where a palette's colour is too faint to read as text on its own
background (below WCAG AA, 4.5:1), the KDE colour scheme moves it toward the
scheme's text colour until it passes; every other colour is the palette's own.


